## Angular workspace boundary

- This is an Angular 22 standalone, strict, zoneless workspace using the 2025 filename style.
- The Angular workspace root is `{frontend.root}`. It must not contain a root `src/` application.
- Applications are ordered as `{angular.applicationNames}` and live only under `{frontend.appsRoot}/<application>/`.
- Reusable Angular libraries are ordered as `{angular.libraryNames}` and live only under `{frontend.libsRoot}/<library>/`.
- Keep `src/main.ts` focused on selected integration setup and Angular bootstrap. The root component and application configuration may coordinate application-wide startup, layout, and routing, but not ordinary feature behavior.
- Organize product behavior beneath `src/app/features/<capability>/`, using names that describe what users can do. Do not introduce mandatory `core/` or `domains/` folders or global `components/`, `services/`, and `types/` buckets.
- Create `layout/`, `startup/`, `config/`, `shared/`, and test folders only when their boundary is actually needed. Do not add empty folder trees for possible future work.
- Keep the root route table as a small application entry map. Prefer lazy `loadComponent` or `loadChildren` boundaries for non-initial capabilities, and let a large capability own `features/<capability>/<capability>.routes.ts`; small route groups may remain in the root table.
- Use `src/app/shared/` only for code reused by multiple capabilities in one application. Move cross-application UI, utilities, and other capabilities beneath `{frontend.libsRoot}` only when they have a real reusable package boundary.
- Keep application features and platform adapters inside their owning application; never import another application's source.
- Keep app-specific static assets under the application's `public/` boundary when they are needed.
- Treat generated artifacts and `dist/` as outputs, never source ownership.
- The frontend `package.json`, `angular.json`, and TypeScript configurations are assembled configuration boundaries. Add stack-specific fields through their owning puzzle pieces.
- Routing is `{angular.routingMode}`, SSR is `{angular.ssr}`, and component styles use `{angular.styleMode}`.
- No test runner or spec configuration is selected here. Follow the selected testing-layout guidance; this Angular piece creates no test folders.
- WebQuark integration is `{webquark.integrationEnabled}`. When it is enabled, read `.agents/shared/webquark.md`, reuse WebQuark components before custom replacements, and keep the shared foundation import before application-global styles. When it is disabled, do not add WebQuark imports to application source or styles.
